From ec05df260a1502530d5a97ef632f4f9185a96ccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixvolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:55:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: MMQ tiles stage activations 8 B-aligned with padded LDS
 rows; R10 follow-ups (expert paths guarded, A/B switches)

MMQ (all repacked tiles: Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K, Q5_1, Q8_0, nibble formats, Q3_K):
- Activations are staged in LDS as a 40 B {float d, float s, int8 qs[32]} instead of the 36 B
  block_q8_1: with qs at offset 4 every activation word read split into b32 pairs (72 ds_read2_b32
  and 83 waits per inner loop vs 32 b64); the scales are widened once at staging. With 5 blocks
  per token row the 200 B row stride keeps the b64 reads conflict-free. (Found by the reinstinct
  session in the ISA diff, crossport.)
- LDS weight and scale rows are padded (int8 rows 128 -> 144 B, uint4/float2 rows [BK] -> [BK+1]):
  a 16-lane column read of the old layout hit one or two banks (16-way for the int8 rows); now 2-way.
  Standalone, the Q4_0 tile goes 8.8 -> 10.0 (staging) -> 11.25 TMAC/s (padding), identical to
  reinstinct's mmq_gemm_q4_0_repacked on the same buffers. test-repack-bench at 2048 tokens:
  q5_K 7.75 -> 9.4, q6_K 6.95 -> 8.3, q4_0 8.96 -> 9.9, IQ family 8.8 -> 9.7, MoE Q5_1 down
  3.3 -> 4.6 TMAC/s; Qwen3.5-4B pp512 UD-Q4_K_XL 1614 -> 1710, Q4_0 1708 -> 1849, Q5_K_M 1520 -> 1736;
  Flash-Next pp2048 1267 -> 1335, pp8192 1965 -> 2055, decode unchanged. Results are bit-identical
  to the previous tiles (--check nmse unchanged; same dot order).

R10 follow-ups:
- The HAS_IDS (expert) paths of the Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 matvecs and the Q4_K GLU are back on the
  guarded per-row loop; only the dense paths keep the clamp + hoisted loads (reinstinct measured
  Gemma 26B-A4B decode -13% with the expert paths hoisted).
- The generic Q8_0 matvec hoist is K-gated to ne00 <= 3072: it wins at K = 2560/2816
  (2560x10240 74 -> 57 us, 2816x4096 38 -> 33) and loses at K = 4096 (2816 rows: +4% here,
  +30% on a second MI50).
- A/B switches for the in-model attribution of the remaining 26B delta: GGML_CUDA_NO_KQ_HOIST=1
  (dense K-quant matvecs and GLU back to the guarded loop; Qwen3.5-4B UD-Q4_K_XL tg64 136 -> 119
  with it) and GGML_CUDA_NO_Q8_HOIST=1. --check passes with every switch setting.

